# SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION

## Project Title: Cybersecurity Mentorship Platform

## Version: 2.0

## Focus: Cybersecurity-Only Guided Mentorship System

---

# 1. INTRODUCTION

## 1.1 Purpose

This document defines the requirements for a cybersecurity-focused mentorship platform where learners apply, get reviewed, receive access, choose or are assigned one cybersecurity path, study guided content, watch embedded YouTube videos, view slides, take quizzes, and progress through structured learning.

The platform is not a general academy. It is a selective cybersecurity mentorship system.

## 1.2 Scope

The system will support:

* Cybersecurity-only mentorship paths
* Application-based access
* Coupon-based login
* Single active path per mentee
* Admin-controlled path assignment
* YouTube-based video learning
* Slide-based lesson viewing
* Quizzes after lessons or modules
* Guided progress tracking
* Completion-based next-path assignment
* Admin management of mentees, paths, videos, slides, quizzes, and progress

---

# 2. PRODUCT VISION

The platform should feel like a guided cybersecurity mentorship journey.

A mentee should feel:

* “I know exactly what to learn next.”
* “I am not watching random videos.”
* “My learning is structured.”
* “My mentor controls my path.”
* “When I finish one path, I can be assigned another.”

The system should not feel like:

* a generic LMS
* a course marketplace
* a random file library
* an open YouTube playlist

---

# 3. CORE USER FLOW

## 3.1 Visitor Flow

Visitor lands on mentorship page
→ explores cybersecurity paths
→ applies for mentorship
→ waits for review
→ receives approval and coupon
→ logs in
→ accesses assigned cybersecurity path

## 3.2 Mentee Flow

Mentee logs in
→ sees active cybersecurity path
→ watches YouTube lessons
→ views slides
→ completes quizzes
→ tracks progress
→ completes path
→ waits for admin to assign next path

## 3.3 Admin Flow

Admin logs in
→ reviews applications
→ approves/rejects applicants
→ generates coupon
→ assigns one cybersecurity path
→ monitors progress
→ reviews completion
→ assigns next path when ready

---

# 4. CORE BUSINESS RULES

BR-1: The platform focuses only on cybersecurity mentorship.

BR-2: A mentee can have only one active cybersecurity path at a time.

BR-3: A mentee may choose a preferred path during application, but final assignment is controlled by admin.

BR-4: Admin can assign another path only after the current path is completed or manually closed.

BR-5: A user cannot access mentorship content without approval and valid coupon login.

BR-6: YouTube videos must be embedded inside the platform so views count on YouTube.

BR-7: Slides must be viewable inside the platform.

BR-8: Quizzes must be attached to modules or lessons.

BR-9: Progress must be tracked per path, module, lesson, video, slide, and quiz.

BR-10: Admin can unlock, revoke, pause, or complete a mentee’s assigned path.

---

# 5. USER CLASSES

## 5.1 Visitor

Can:

* view public mentorship page
* preview cybersecurity paths
* apply

Cannot:

* access lessons
* watch protected learning videos inside dashboard
* take quizzes
* access slides

## 5.2 Applicant

Can:

* submit application
* view pending status

Cannot:

* access mentorship dashboard until approved

## 5.3 Mentee

Can:

* access assigned cybersecurity path
* watch YouTube lesson videos
* view slides
* complete quizzes
* view progress
* book sessions if enabled

Cannot:

* access unassigned paths
* self-unlock another path
* skip required quizzes if progression rules apply

## 5.4 Admin / Mentor

Can:

* review applications
* approve or reject users
* create coupons
* assign paths
* manage cybersecurity content
* upload or link slides
* add YouTube video links
* create quizzes
* monitor progress
* assign next path

---

# 6. CYBERSECURITY MENTORSHIP PATHS

The system will support multiple cybersecurity paths.

Example paths:

1. Introduction to Cybersecurity
2. Network Security
3. SOC Analyst Foundation
4. Ethical Hacking Foundations
5. Web Application Security
6. Cloud Security Basics
7. Digital Forensics Introduction
8. Incident Response
9. Governance, Risk, and Compliance
10. Cybersecurity Career Preparation

Each path will contain:

* overview
* outcomes
* modules
* lessons
* YouTube videos
* slides
* quizzes
* completion rules

---

# 7. SINGLE ACTIVE PATH MODEL

## 7.1 Description

Each mentee can only study one active path at a time.

Example:

A student starts:

Introduction to Cybersecurity

After completion, admin may assign:

SOC Analyst Foundation

This creates a controlled guided journey.

## 7.2 Functional Requirements

FR-1: System shall allow a mentee to have only one active path.

FR-2: System shall allow completed paths to remain visible as history.

FR-3: System shall prevent a mentee from opening unassigned paths.

FR-4: Admin shall be able to assign a new path after completion.

FR-5: Admin shall be able to override and assign another path manually.

FR-6: Mentee may request the next path after completion.

---

# 8. APPLICATION SYSTEM

## 8.1 Application Fields

The application form shall collect:

* full name
* email
* phone
* country
* age
* cybersecurity experience level
* preferred path
* reason for applying
* career goal
* weekly availability
* device/internet access
* password
* confirmation password

## 8.2 Application Status

Application statuses:

* Pending
* Under Review
* Approved
* Rejected

## 8.3 Functional Requirements

FR-7: Visitor shall apply before accessing mentorship.

FR-8: Admin shall review applications.

FR-9: Admin shall approve or reject applications.

FR-10: On approval, system shall generate coupon.

FR-11: Approved applicant shall be assigned one cybersecurity path.

---

# 9. COUPON-BASED LOGIN

## 9.1 Login Fields

Mentee login requires:

* email or username
* password
* coupon code

## 9.2 Functional Requirements

FR-12: System shall block login without coupon.

FR-13: System shall validate coupon before granting access.

FR-14: Coupon shall be linked to approved user.

FR-15: Coupon shall be linked to access type: Cybersecurity Mentorship.

FR-16: System shall reject expired, inactive, or invalid coupons.

---

# 10. CONTENT STRUCTURE

## 10.1 Hierarchy

Cybersecurity Path
→ Module
→ Lesson
→ YouTube Video
→ Slides
→ Quiz
→ Completion

## 10.2 Path Entity

Each path shall contain:

* title
* slug
* description
* level
* estimated duration
* outcomes
* modules
* active status
* order

## 10.3 Module Entity

Each module shall contain:

* title
* description
* order
* lessons
* quiz
* unlock rule

## 10.4 Lesson Entity

Each lesson shall contain:

* title
* description
* YouTube video link
* slide resource
* reading content
* estimated duration
* completion status

---

# 11. YOUTUBE VIDEO LEARNING SYSTEM

## 11.1 Description

All platform videos shall come from YouTube. The platform embeds the videos so learners can watch inside the mentorship dashboard while YouTube views still increase.

## 11.2 Functional Requirements

FR-17: Admin shall add YouTube video URL or video ID to a lesson.

FR-18: System shall embed YouTube video inside lesson page.

FR-19: Mentee shall watch video within the platform.

FR-20: System shall store video metadata including title, duration, video ID, and lesson ID.

FR-21: System shall allow admin to reorder videos inside modules.

FR-22: System shall allow a lesson to contain one or more videos.

FR-23: System shall not host videos directly unless future requirements change.

## 11.3 Video Lesson UI

The video page shall include:

* embedded YouTube player
* lesson title
* lesson summary
* slides panel
* next lesson button
* mark as complete button
* quiz button if available
* progress indicator

---

# 12. SLIDE VIEWING SYSTEM

## 12.1 Description

Slides are used as structured lesson materials. A mentee should view slides directly in the platform.

## 12.2 Supported Slide Types

The system may support:

* PDF slides
* image-based slides
* embedded Google Slides
* HTML lesson slides
* uploaded presentation files converted to PDF later

## 12.3 Functional Requirements

FR-24: Admin shall upload or link slides to a lesson.

FR-25: Mentee shall view slides inside the lesson page.

FR-26: Slide viewer shall allow next/previous navigation.

FR-27: Slide viewer shall work on desktop and mobile.

FR-28: System shall track whether the slide lesson has been completed.

## 12.4 Slide UI Requirements

Slide viewer shall include:

* slide title
* progress count
* next/previous controls
* fullscreen option if possible
* related video beside or above slides
* quiz access after lesson completion

---

# 13. QUIZ SYSTEM

## 13.1 Description

Quizzes validate understanding before progression.

## 13.2 Question Types

The system shall support:

* multiple choice
* true/false
* short answer

Future support:

* scenario-based cybersecurity questions
* lab-based questions
* practical SOC analysis tasks

## 13.3 Functional Requirements

FR-29: Admin shall create quizzes per lesson or module.

FR-30: Quiz shall have passing score.

FR-31: System shall auto-grade objective questions.

FR-32: System shall record quiz attempts.

FR-33: System shall display score after submission.

FR-34: System shall unlock next module only after passing quiz if required.

FR-35: Admin shall configure retake policy.

## 13.4 Quiz UI

Quiz page shall show:

* quiz title
* number of questions
* progress through quiz
* selected answers
* submit button
* score result
* pass/fail message
* retry option if allowed

---

# 14. PROGRESS TRACKING

## 14.1 Description

The platform must track mentee progress across assigned path.

## 14.2 Tracked Items

The system shall track:

* path progress
* module progress
* lesson completion
* video completion status
* slide completion status
* quiz attempts
* quiz pass/fail status
* current lesson
* completed paths
* assigned next path status

## 14.3 Functional Requirements

FR-36: System shall calculate progress percentage.

FR-37: Mentee shall see current progress.

FR-38: Admin shall see progress per mentee.

FR-39: System shall mark path complete when all required modules are complete.

FR-40: System shall notify admin when mentee completes a path.

---

# 15. MENTEE DASHBOARD

## 15.1 Dashboard Purpose

The dashboard should answer:

“What should I do next?”

## 15.2 Dashboard Sections

The mentee dashboard shall display:

* active cybersecurity path
* current module
* next lesson
* progress percentage
* pending quiz
* completed modules
* locked modules
* mentorship session button
* path completion status

## 15.3 UI Requirements

The dashboard should feel:

* guided
* clean
* interactive
* structured
* similar to NetAcad-style progression

It should not feel like a folder of random files.

---

# 16. PATH VIEW

## 16.1 Description

The path page shows the complete structure of the assigned path.

## 16.2 Required Elements

The path view shall include:

* path title
* path description
* expected outcome
* module list
* locked/unlocked states
* completion status
* progress bar
* continue button

## 16.3 Module States

Modules may be:

* locked
* available
* in progress
* completed

---

# 17. LESSON VIEW

## 17.1 Description

The lesson view is where mentees consume learning content.

## 17.2 Required Elements

Each lesson page shall include:

* lesson title
* embedded YouTube video
* slide viewer
* lesson notes
* completion button
* next/previous navigation
* quiz link
* progress indicator

---

# 18. ADMIN DASHBOARD

## 18.1 Admin Core Sections

Admin dashboard shall include:

* overview
* applications
* mentees
* cybersecurity paths
* modules
* lessons
* videos
* slides
* quizzes
* progress
* coupons
* bookings

## 18.2 Admin Capabilities

Admin can:

* approve applications
* create coupon
* assign first path
* view mentee progress
* create cybersecurity path
* add modules
* add YouTube videos
* upload/link slides
* create quizzes
* assign next path
* pause or revoke access

---

# 19. PATH ASSIGNMENT SYSTEM

## 19.1 Description

Admin controls which path a mentee studies.

## 19.2 Functional Requirements

FR-41: Admin shall assign one active path to a mentee.

FR-42: Admin shall view completed paths before assigning new one.

FR-43: Admin shall assign next path after completion.

FR-44: Admin shall manually override active path if necessary.

FR-45: System shall prevent duplicate active paths.

FR-46: System shall store assignment history.

---

# 20. CONTENT SEEDING SYSTEM

## 20.1 Description

Existing cybersecurity documents and quizzes from the resources folder should be converted into structured mentorship content.

## 20.2 Functional Requirements

FR-47: System shall read local cybersecurity resource documents.

FR-48: System shall convert documents into structured path/module/lesson records.

FR-49: System shall extract or preserve quizzes from the end of documents.

FR-50: System shall seed structured content into Firestore.

FR-51: System shall avoid duplicate seeding.

FR-52: Admin shall be able to edit seeded content later.

---

